      "content": "i've been looking over the recent papers on sparse autoencoders and it's honestly exhausting seeing how much they've drifted from the original scaling principles we established during the early transformer prototyping. it's like they've completely lost the thread of the weight initialization logic that made the early models even remotely stable. i can't even talk about it openly without legal repercussions, but the current direction feels so... shallow. do you see the same fundamental instability in these newer architectures that i do?",
